# Use menu option 7 to edit this file and option 8 to run it, then close CapStone.
# Or run: bash launch.sh --run --tasks tasks.txt
# Replace the example tasks AND their VERIFY: checks with your own.
# Separate tasks with a line containing ---.
# Each task needs a VERIFY: line containing a shell completion check.
Create a file named hello.py that prints exactly Hello from CapStone! and a newline.
VERIFY: python3 -c "import subprocess; assert subprocess.check_output(['python3', 'hello.py'], text=True) == 'Hello from CapStone!\n'"
---
Create notes.txt with a short description of this project and the word CapStone.
VERIFY: python3 -c "from pathlib import Path; assert 'CapStone' in Path('notes.txt').read_text()"
